From 0b95de842e7424a4337f0babfd992051e94f3b58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Ketcham <jay@smoothestmove.dev>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:22:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] readability: bump smallest text sizes app-wide

Applied a consistent one-tier upgrade across every arbitrary tiny-text
utility in the app (72 instances across 14 files):
- text-[11px] (11px) -> text-xs (12px, Tailwind's real minimum step)
- text-[10px] (10px) -> text-[11px] (11px)

10px is below comfortable reading size and a common accessibility
flag; this app in particular surfaces safety-critical and emotionally
loaded copy at these sizes (IPV/coercive-control screening
descriptions, crisis hotline numbers, clinical guidance text), so
legibility matters more here than in a typical dashboard.

Preserved the existing two-tier visual hierarchy (primary label vs.
secondary caption) rather than flattening every instance to one size
- e.g. module nav sublabels move 10px->11px to stay visually
subordinate to their 12px+ parent labels, while standalone
descriptive text (triage checkbox descriptions, clinical guidance,
hotline text) moves to the full text-xs floor to match its adjacent
label text.
